        "OmicsLM: A Multimodal Large Language Model for Multi-Sample Omics Reasoning"
      ],
      "section_id": "sec_0001",
      "text_sha256": "154d424e1f32f00a38396683fb4b3fbad0cb6d72b122c2085a5fe28808fbd0ae"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": 3,
      "heading_path": [
        "OmicsLM: A Multimodal Large Language Model for Multi-Sample Omics Reasoning",
        "Abstract"
      ],
      "section_id": "sec_0002",
      "text_sha256": "6b9f65ea6d84ed96e9237c50dfcd07abf79d9da7f8663ab3011972ddca2702ef"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": 2,
      "heading_path": [
        "1 Introduction"
      ],
      "section_id": "sec_0003",
      "text_sha256": "25cd79b6394524216a6c64678e7d1d52a60b3db75109b78492ce74b7f6d8a565"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": 3,
      "heading_path": [
        "1 Introduction",
        "We present the design of a multi-task instruction-tuning corpus that unifies over 70 task types across diverse datasets (e.g., HCA, TCGA, scPerturb-seq, DepMap) into a standardized conversational format. This broad task mixture spans annotation, clinical prediction, perturbation, essentiality, network reasoning, and open-ended biological interpretation, giving OmicsLM richer supervision for building general omics knowledge."
      ],
      "section_id": "sec_0004",
      "text_sha256": "f3bb23c94a495ca7a6cc8ee83457e4bfd9342b17d367d0af55a38a9e75376170"
    },
    {
      "heading_level": 3,
      "heading_path": [
        "1 Introduction",
        "Wedemonstrate that OmicsLM achieves strong performance across a wide array of biological benchmarks, providing a unified foundation for conversational, omics-informed biological research."
      ],
      "section_id": "sec_0005",
      "text_sha256": "a2eec1b1f92e2101db9c7509359e0475b78b27a2eb44769308d114c155ab51d9"
    },
